# Kebu Master Engineering Instruction

Full contract: `docs/product/KEBU-MASTER-ENGINEERING-INSTRUCTION.md` · **Product Architect:** `docs/product/KEBU-PRODUCT-ARCHITECT-PHASE.md` · Summary: `docs/product/ENGINEERING-MANDATE.md` · Status: `docs/IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS.md`

## Non-negotiables

Kebu is **NOT** a prototype, mock UI, or “looks done” demo. **No MVP-looking UI** unless explicitly requested. **Fewer complete features > many fake screens.**

Every feature = full chain:

**USER → UI → state → API → logic → Supabase → DB/storage/auth → response → UI → refresh persists**

**Supabase:** Auth · Postgres · **RLS** · Storage · migrations only · never service role in browser · never bypass RLS.

## Before code

**Product Architect Phase first** for new major surfaces — blueprint before code (`kebu-product-architect.mdc`).

**Inspect first** — framework, schema, migrations, auth, routes, APIs, tests, broken/disconnected paths. **Do not** duplicate existing systems. Plan concisely, then implement **one assigned slice only**.

## One vertical slice

FEATURE → DATABASE → BACKEND → FRONTEND → SUPABASE → TEST → DEBUG → **COMPLETE**

Forbidden: all-pages-first · all-APIs-first · giant schema-first · fake buttons/success · hardcoded persistence · mock prod DB ops.

## Dependency rule (stop and repair)

If you discover a **previous slice is incomplete, broken, or disconnected**, **STOP the current task** and **repair that dependency first**.

**Do not** build new functionality on top of broken functionality.

Order: identify blocking defect → fix root cause → verify end-to-end → **then** resume the assigned slice.

## Error honesty

**Never hide an error** — suppress console/network failures, swallow exceptions, empty catch blocks, or fake success — **simply to make the UI appear functional.**

Surface errors honestly (UI + logs). Fix root cause or label **BLOCKED** / **NOT IMPLEMENTED** with the missing dependency.

## Build → Design QA → audit → repair (mandatory loop)

1. **Implement Slice N end-to-end** — do not start Slice N+1  
2. **Design QA** — open running app; fix spacing/hierarchy/density/polish until standard met  
3. **Adversarial audit** — trace every user action FE→Supabase→FE; fix bugs, authz, RLS, persistence, errors, tests  
4. **Update IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS** — then next slice  

## Definition of done

FE + BE + Supabase + migration + RLS + auth + authz + persist + refresh + all states + validation + tests + build. Missing any applicable item = **INCOMPLETE**. Not done = label **NOT IMPLEMENTED** or **BLOCKED** — never fake success.

## Bugs

Discover → reproduce → **root cause** (FE→API→Supabase→DB) → fix → regression test when practical. **Never ignore, suppress, or paper over** — including hiding errors so the UI looks fine.

## Foundation priority

**Kebu Account + Kebu ID + workspace/business + Supabase** — Builder, Cloud, Search, Mail, Analytics, Opportunity OS, Score all depend on this.

## Product law (do not violate while building)

- **Opportunity OS** ≠ **Kebu Opportunity OS** — separate products; API integration only  
- **Personal Kebu** (free) ≠ **Business Kebu** (Kebu ID workspace) — one login  
- **Kebu Search** = real engine; AI on top with citations — never chat-as-search  
- **Builder** = structured schema — not static HTML dump; not Shopify clone checklist  
- **Nav only when real** — no fake future-product dashboards  

## After every slice

Typecheck · lint · **`npm run ci`** · migration/RLS check · manual journey · console/network · refresh · unauthorized user denied.

**CI failure → deployment stops** — `docs/CI_PIPELINE.md`

**REAL FUNCTIONALITY > NUMBER OF FEATURES.**
